text	**Change of a partner's rate**  Thank you for your answer about rate changes. We will build it as you describe. When you change the rate of a partner, the new rate applies by default only to customers that the partner brings after the change. The commissions on the partner's current customers stay as they are. The dialog where you change the rate also has an "All customers" choice. Use it only when you want the new rate to apply to the partner's current customers too. If you do not select it, the current customers keep their old rate.  ---  Two points before you send this:  - **This adds something to what the client asked for.** Their letter says the commissions on current customers "stay as they are", and it does not mention an "All customers" choice. The paragraph presents that choice as optional, so it agrees with their rule. If you want them to approve the choice, add a question such as: "Please tell us if you do not want this choice." - **Partner history (point 3 of their letter).** If the history will show which choice was used for each rate change, say so here. I left it out because we have not decided it.
